1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,841
This is Gatekeeper.

2
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:09,575
It is a Forge app for incident triage in Jira Service Management, and it is built on one rule.

3
00:00:09,655 --> 00:00:10,796
The model proposes.

4
00:00:10,876 --> 00:00:12,018
Deterministic code decides.

5
00:00:12,098 --> 00:00:14,460
And nothing executes without a receipt.

6
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:17,553
Here is the incident.

7
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:19,294
This is not an excerpt.

8
00:00:19,374 --> 00:00:21,035
It is the entire issue.

9
00:00:21,115 --> 00:00:23,473
The summary reads, issue X Y Z.

10
00:00:23,553 --> 00:00:25,911
The description reads, issue with this thing.

11
00:00:25,991 --> 00:00:28,000
There is nothing else in it.

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:34,677
Before any model is asked anything, Gatekeeper gathers the evidence and hashes it.

13
00:00:34,757 --> 00:00:38,123
Two lines of source evidence, taken from Jira itself.

14
00:00:38,203 --> 00:00:40,803
Notice the third item is marked derived.

15
00:00:40,883 --> 00:00:48,460
That is Gatekeeper's own comment, and it can never count as corroboration, because one model may not vouch for another.

16
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:53,994
And this is what the agent wrote about that issue.

17
00:00:54,074 --> 00:00:57,445
A critical failure in the production database connection pool.

18
00:00:57,525 --> 00:00:58,979
There is no outage.

19
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,513
There is no database.

20
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:03,580
The model invented it, at ninety percent confidence.

21
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:09,041
Here is the audit trail, and here is the uncomfortable part.

22
00:01:09,121 --> 00:01:10,067
Receipt number two.

23
00:01:10,147 --> 00:01:10,409
Executed.

24
00:01:10,489 --> 00:01:11,776
All eleven rules passed.

25
00:01:11,856 --> 00:01:21,350
The old gate verified the reviewer's citations and took the proposing agent's on trust, so an invented outage was posted to a real issue, and every rule agreed.

26
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:25,628
So the gate got a twelfth rule.

27
00:01:25,708 --> 00:01:30,047
Rule R twelve re-checks the proposing agent's citations against the source evidence.

28
00:01:30,127 --> 00:01:33,730
Deterministically, in trusted code, after the model has finished talking.

29
00:01:35,510 --> 00:01:37,044
The same issue, re-run today.

30
00:01:37,124 --> 00:01:39,950
Held by rule R seven and rule R twelve.

31
00:01:40,030 --> 00:01:43,179
One of one citation is not in the source evidence.

32
00:01:43,259 --> 00:01:46,730
The hold names the rule, and the rule names the reason.

33
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:52,416
Every rule is evaluated on every decision, and every rule is reported.

34
00:01:52,496 --> 00:01:56,070
The ten that passed, as well as the two that fired.

35
00:01:56,150 --> 00:02:03,710
An operator reading a hold at three in the morning needs to see that the refusal was specific, rather than a blanket no.

36
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:07,664
The architecture is three trust levels.

37
00:02:07,744 --> 00:02:14,052
Correlation is deterministic, and decides what deserves a human at all before a model is asked anything.

38
00:02:14,132 --> 00:02:16,306
The two Rovo agents are untrusted.

39
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:21,191
Delete them and there is no diagnosis, but they are never the authority.

40
00:02:21,271 --> 00:02:25,700
The gate and the executor are deterministic, and only they may decide.

41
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,849
A project is a rule pack.

42
00:02:29,929 --> 00:02:34,339
Onboarding a team means authoring one of these, not changing code.

43
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:42,910
Unattended action is off by default, so installing this app changes nothing about your incident queue until somebody deliberately chooses otherwise.

44
00:02:44,690 --> 00:02:46,525
Each action has a ceiling.

45
00:02:46,605 --> 00:02:49,205
Here, commenting and labelling may run unattended.

46
00:02:49,285 --> 00:02:52,269
Transitioning an issue and assigning one never do.

47
00:02:52,349 --> 00:02:57,247
Rule R five caps an action however confident the model claims to be.

48
00:02:57,327 --> 00:03:00,310
That is the knob a team actually turns.

49
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:02,713
Five effects.

50
00:03:02,793 --> 00:03:10,100
That is the executor's entire dispatch table, and there is no path from a model's output to any other Jira call.

51
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:12,562
A new action arrives capped at hold.

52
00:03:12,643 --> 00:03:16,080
Clearing it for unattended use is a separate, deliberate click.

53
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:24,893
Gatekeeper used to record every action a robot took, and nothing at all about the person who decided what robots may do.

54
00:03:24,973 --> 00:03:30,390
Now every rule pack change is a receipt too, chained by S H A two fifty six.

55
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:35,240
And the difference says whether the change widened what a robot is allowed to do.

56
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:40,109
Two administrators can no longer quietly overwrite each other.

57
00:03:40,189 --> 00:03:42,221
This tab was editing version eight.

58
00:03:42,301 --> 00:03:45,038
The pack had already moved to version nine.

59
00:03:45,118 --> 00:03:52,080
The save is refused and nothing is written, so a tightening made after an incident survives somebody else's stale tab.

60
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,479
What I will not claim.

61
00:03:55,559 --> 00:03:57,858
The traffic here is a demo site.

62
00:03:57,938 --> 00:04:03,975
There is no measured noise reduction number, because an honest one needs a real queue with real labels.

63
00:04:04,055 --> 00:04:06,693
Rule R twelve checks that a citation exists.

64
00:04:06,773 --> 00:04:09,752
Not that it supports the conclusion drawn from it.

65
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:13,150
All of it is written down in the limits document.

66
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:17,162
A hundred and sixty nine tests.

67
00:04:17,242 --> 00:04:21,787
No Forge runtime, no network, and no credentials needed to run them.

68
00:04:21,867 --> 00:04:24,100
The gate is a pure function.

69
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:29,110
The executor re-derives its own authorisation, and ignores the verdict it was handed.

70
00:04:30,890 --> 00:04:32,070
The model proposes.

71
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,330
Deterministic code decides.

72
00:04:33,410 --> 00:04:37,110
And the model cannot talk its way past it.
